  "captions": [
    {"start": 0.433, "end": 3.473, "lines": ["So one of our first steps","in the epidemiologic portion"]},
    {"start": 3.473, "end": 8.753, "lines": ["of the investigation was to create a broad","hypothesis generating questionnaire."]},
    {"start": 8.753, "end": 12.033, "lines": ["So for that, we wanted to know","what foods people were eating,"]},
    {"start": 12.033, "end": 15.633, "lines": ["what water sources people drank from,","whether people treated their water"]},
    {"start": 15.633, "end": 17.473, "lines": ["at home, if people had attended"]},
    {"start": 17.473, "end": 20.753, "lines": ["any large community gatherings,","or if they had had recent animal"]},
    {"start": 20.753, "end": 23.488, "lines": ["contact. And so,","to distribute those questionnaires,"]},
    {"start": 23.488, "end": 25.248, "lines": ["we used a lot of different methods."]},
    {"start": 25.248, "end": 26.768, "lines": ["We used social media, we used"]},
    {"start": 26.768, "end": 31.328, "lines": ["the local health department's website,","email, and door-to-door canvassing."]},
    {"start": 31.328, "end": 34.368, "lines": ["Then, we needed to analyze the results","of our questionnaire,"]},
    {"start": 34.368, "end": 39.088, "lines": ["and we calculated odds ratios","for the different possible exposures."]},
    {"start": 39.088, "end": 43.488, "lines": ["So, we had 138 questionnaires come back","to us, and from those,"]},
    {"start": 43.488, "end": 47.104, "lines": ["we identified 64 cases","of campobacteriosis."]},
    {"start": 47.104, "end": 50.864, "lines": ["And even that is probably a bit of the tip","of the iceberg because obviously we"]},
    {"start": 50.864, "end": 53.024, "lines": ["weren't able to reach everybody","in the town,"]},
    {"start": 53.024, "end": 57.344, "lines": ["and some people might have had more mild","illnesses that they didn't recognize"]},
    {"start": 57.344, "end": 58.384, "lines": ["or report."]},
    {"start": 58.384, "end": 64.144, "lines": ["Even as it was, 64 people, that's a huge","percentage of a town of only about 330."]},
    {"start": 64.144, "end": 69.824, "lines": ["And we found from that that municipal","water exposure was strongly associated"]},
    {"start": 69.824, "end": 71.504, "lines": ["with illness."]},
    {"start": 71.504, "end": 75.304, "lines": ["No other exposures had statistically","significant associations."]},
    {"start": 75.568, "end": 77.488, "lines": ["Drinking water is not a common source"]},
    {"start": 77.488, "end": 80.608, "lines": ["of outbreaks like this,","as Dr. Jansen notes."]},
    {"start": 80.608, "end": 82.608, "lines": ["Most campobacteriosis outbreaks"]},
    {"start": 82.608, "end": 86.128, "lines": ["are eventually linked to food,","usually dairy and poultry."]},
    {"start": 86.128, "end": 88.288, "lines": ["So, water was the surprising cause."]},
    {"start": 88.288, "end": 92.688, "lines": ["Then, our investigation used both","epidemiologic and environmental methods."]},
    {"start": 92.688, "end": 95.088, "lines": ["So, as part","of the environmental investigation,"]},
    {"start": 95.088, "end": 99.728, "lines": ["the town's water system was evaluated","and water testing was done."]},
    {"start": 99.728, "end": 103.488, "lines": ["And that testing was positive","for coliforms, which suggested"]},
    {"start": 103.488, "end": 105.408, "lines": ["possible water contamination."]},
    {"start": 105.408, "end": 109.488, "lines": ["The town issued a boil water advisory,","and then there was a request"]},
    {"start": 109.488, "end": 111.648, "lines": ["for specialized campy bacteria testing."]},
    {"start": 111.648, "end": 113.648, "lines": ["Now, that's not normally available"]},
    {"start": 113.648, "end": 117.008, "lines": ["in Nebraska, so we had to reach","out to CDC for that testing."]},
    {"start": 117.008, "end": 121.168, "lines": ["So, CDC was able to guide our colleagues","at the Nebraska Department of Environment"]},
    {"start": 121.168, "end": 125.328, "lines": ["and Energy through the collection","of these samples. So, six large-volume"]},
    {"start": 125.328, "end": 128.608, "lines": ["dead-end ultra-filtration water samples,","and those were collected"]},
    {"start": 128.608, "end": 131.968, "lines": ["from the two active town wells","and some other important sites"]},
    {"start": 131.968, "end": 134.208, "lines": ["in the town's water distribution system."]},
    {"start": 134.208, "end": 138.448, "lines": ["And then CDC was able to perform","the Campbell bacter specific DNA testing"]},
    {"start": 138.448, "end": 143.488, "lines": ["and culture on those samples, as well","as the microbial source tracking."]},
    {"start": 143.488, "end": 145.328, "lines": ["This microbial source tracking"]},
    {"start": 145.328, "end": 148.992, "lines": ["was a unique and important part","of this investigation."]},
    {"start": 148.992, "end": 152.032, "lines": ["So, microbial source tracking is a PCR"]},
    {"start": 152.032, "end": 157.152, "lines": ["technique that can identify bacteria","molecular markers that are unique"]},
    {"start": 157.152, "end": 162.272, "lines": ["to humans, ruminants like cows","and deer, and bird feces."]},
    {"start": 162.272, "end": 165.952, "lines": ["And we were interested","in those because humans, ruminants,"]},
    {"start": 165.952, "end": 169.952, "lines": ["and birds, those are known environmental","fecal shutters of Campylbacter."]},
    {"start": 169.952, "end": 174.112, "lines": ["So, there were six samples,","and one was positive by PCR"]},
    {"start": 174.112, "end": 176.928, "lines": ["for presence of Campylbacter DNA."]},
    {"start": 176.928, "end": 180.688, "lines": ["And then the microbial source","tracking detected avian-specific"]},
    {"start": 180.688, "end": 183.168, "lines": ["fecal rRNA genomic material."]},
    {"start": 183.168, "end": 185.568, "lines": ["So, those findings together suggested"]},
    {"start": 185.568, "end": 189.248, "lines": ["that the water contamination likely came","from bird feces."]},
    {"start": 189.248, "end": 191.248, "lines": ["And microbial source tracking proved"]},
    {"start": 191.248, "end": 193.648, "lines": ["to be tremendously helpful","because it allowed us"]},
    {"start": 193.648, "end": 196.368, "lines": ["to link the contamination specifically","to bird feces."]},
    {"start": 196.368, "end": 198.128, "lines": ["And that led us right to the source"]},
    {"start": 198.128, "end": 201.848, "lines": ["and enabled us to take that action","to stop the contamination."]},
    {"start": 202.208, "end": 205.808, "lines": ["Knowing that bird feces was the likely","source of contamination,"]},
    {"start": 205.808, "end": 208.448, "lines": ["the investigators then looked","into how bird feces"]},
    {"start": 208.448, "end": 210.268, "lines": ["could have entered the water system."]}
